title: The Troop Trains
subtitle: Everywhere else the strike is over.
view-if: crisis_ruhr = 1 and e20_ruhr_solidarity_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; e20_ruhr_solidarity_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Troop Trains

The rest of Germany has gone back to work. Freikorps volunteers are coming to Münster by train from Berlin, from Pomerania and from Bavaria, and every one of those trains passes through a junction worked by union men.

- @rail: Ask the railwaymen to stop the troop trains.
- @halle: Call the Halle district out again.

@rail
subtitle: Fewer troops will reach Watter. The railwaymen will be sacked for it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_ruhr_watter = Math.max(5, Q.e20_ruhr_watter - 8);
Q.repression += 3;
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
!}

At Hamm and Soest the signalmen walk out. The trains wait a day in the sidings, and some of the volunteers go home.

@halle
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A second front at Leuna and Mansfeld, if the workers there will follow.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
RG.startStrike('halle', true);
Q.e20_ruhr_watter = Math.max(5, Q.e20_ruhr_watter - 4);
RG.district('halle', {militancy: 6, repression: 4});
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
!}

The Leuna works and the Mansfeld pits stop again. Two Freikorps battalions are turned round at Kassel and sent east.
